{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Have you [E]ever been to Richmond in November
When the [G#]cold Virginia rain is coming [A]down
[A]Friends I'm here to tell you it's no [E]pleasure
If you're [F#]all alone and a stranger to this [B]town
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Don't [E]take me wrong I do like East Virginia
And [G#]Richmond's full of [A]hospitality
[A]Except for one Virginia girl I [E]know of
[E]That made a perfect [B]love wreck out of [E]me
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[A]Blue [B]blue Virginia [E]blues
There [A]ain’t no blue like [E]blue Virginia [B]blues
[A]There ain’t no other girls in the [B]whole wide world
Will [E]break your heart like [A]Virginia girls
There's [E]ain’t no blue like [A]blue [B]Virginia [E]blues
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
She called me up in St Paul Minnesota
Said I need you here in Richmond right away
Take the bus and I'll meet you at the station
Bring some clothes I might want you to stay
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
My bus pulled in the station late this evening
There ain’t a soul around this place but me
She must have changed her mind or she's forgotten
And her name ain’t in the phone directory
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
I wish I had the money for a taxi
And a warm and cozy place to lay me down
Instead of standing all alone in Richmond
While the cold Virginia rain is coming down
{end_of_chorus}
